  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>DogSitting à Nice is a boarding service with a dog sitter based in the Fabron neighbourhood of Nice. Its distinctive point, highlighted on its website: since she works from home, your dog is the only dog hosted during its stay and is never left alone. She lives in an apartment, but has a huge, fully fenced, tree-lined park for outings.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Full board costs 18€ per day. She also offers daytime care and daily walks, in Nice, Cannes, Monaco, Cagnes-sur-Mer and Antibes. She accepts dogs that are not house-trained or that bark, but refuses destructive dogs. As with any boarding at a private individual's home, plan a meeting with your dog before booking a stay.</p>
      <p>The website, a small blog, presents the formula as an alternative to large kennels: no boxes, the dog lives "as if at home" and is never left alone. It does not publish vaccination requirements, a minimum length of stay or details of the preliminary meeting: these points are settled by direct contact.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the "single dog" format can be reassuring for a timid animal or one not very sociable with other dogs. The website dates from 2018 and shows no recent update: confirm availability and prices before counting on it.</div>

      <p>Fabron is a residential neighbourhood in western Nice, between the sea and the hills, close to the Promenade des Anglais and a few minutes from Saint-Laurent-du-Var or Cagnes-sur-Mer.</p>
